Why AGPL-3.0-or-later, and not MIT (which this project carried until 2026-08-16):
EsotericOS talks over the network -- LAN nodes that extend one desk across
machines, a clipboard relay, an input portal. The Affero clause (section 13)
closes the one door a plain GPL leaves open: running a modified version to serve
users over a network without ever distributing it. Strong copyleft is the point,
not an afterthought -- the aim is to encroach on corporate capture by making the
free, copyleft solution so good that everyone wants it, and to keep it free.

Third-party components keep their own licences; they are not relicensed by this
